Anatomy & Physiology — Oregon State University (@med-source-osu: 0, is #book, #part-of @medicine-sources) { r_1WEZWZ5YY6797K4EXVYTBJS25N
Lindsay M. Biga and colleagues; Oregon State University and OpenStax. Anatomy & Physiology, 2019 edition. English.

[Authorized source](https://open.oregonstate.education/anatomy/).

The main explanatory textbook. [Begin medicine from zero — a substantial reading progression](../foundations/Reading-from-zero.lingua#r_4FA8H4RKD8T52WY2Z1B8S7XQ50) assigns complete early chapter blocks, a broader whole-body reading, and a whole-book continuation. Later guides deliberately narrow an assignment to named sections or a specific anatomical passage. An explicitly selected passage builds on the broader reading rather than replacing it. The site points to a later edition; these readings identify the 2019 edition and its chapter organization. Use current clinical sources for management questions.

**Alternative web reading:** [OpenStax Anatomy and Physiology 2e](https://openstax.org/books/anatomy-and-physiology-2e/pages/1-introduction) covers the corresponding foundational topics. Match the named section when numbering differs. Its [current licensing information](https://help.openstax.org/s/article/Licensing-information-of-OpenStax-textbooks) states CC BY-NC-SA; keep its edition and terms distinct from the Oregon State adaptation. No copy of that edition is bundled.

**Access and reuse:** The publisher declares CC BY-SA 4.0 for this adaptation, except where otherwise noted. It adapts an earlier CC BY OpenStax edition. Attribution: Biga et al., Anatomy & Physiology, OpenStax/Oregon State University, 2019; retain component-specific notices. No local copy is supplied. [Licence](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/).

